{"author":{"id":"1949ffc23f11a8cb4f8c42a45c9ad241b49570df9a18687489e9ea78d87c54a3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1779114147,"nonce":"pwIGh1jMJ9+Zq7KYibuG1mfSP9U=","title":"Phase 5a: make Studio workspace the active state owner","message":"## Parent / coordination\n- Roadmap: `fa3978f` — Feedbax/Mandible MVP integration roadmap, Phase 5.\n- Pipeline spec: `0c46f69`.\n- Structural authoring spec: `5378a5d`.\n- Phase 4 completion: `d30d4c2`.\n\n## Problem\nPhase 4 created a durable Studio workspace and a provider-backed train -\u003e eval -\u003e analysis -\u003e report vertical path, but the live frontend still treats `trainingStore.trainingSpec/taskSpec` and other global stores as the source of executable truth. That leaves hidden global-store interpretation paths even though the durable project model now has stage/scenario ownership.\n\n## Scope\nMake `StudioWorkspaceSpec` and active stage/scenario state the active owner for Studio executable drafts:\n\n- Add workspace-store selectors/actions for active stage, active scenario, stage switching, scenario draft updates, task/training/objective updates, collection updates, and draft metadata.\n- Promote current `TrainingSpec`, `TaskSpec`, and loss/objective data into the active train-stage scenario as the primary editable state.\n- Change training/task/loss editing flows to update workspace scenario state directly, with any legacy training-store values treated as view/runtime mirrors rather than ownership.\n- Preserve executed snapshot refs and dirty/version metadata on stages/scenarios.\n- Add focused tests proving edits round-trip through workspace/stage/scenario state and no future/custom stage metadata is dropped.\n\n## Non-goals\n- No full report authoring UI in this slice.\n- No live SSH/RunPod/Modal execution.\n- No Mandible UI work.\n- Do not prioritize old Studio compatibility over the end-state spec; remove or demote legacy ownership paths when they conflict.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- Training/task/loss edits mutate the active train-stage scenario in `workspaceStore`.\n- `buildWorkspaceSnapshot` preserves workspace-owned drafts without reintroducing global-store ownership.\n- Active stage/scenario switching is available through typed store APIs.\n- Tests cover workspace-owned edits, stage switching, and preservation of custom/future stage metadata.\n\n---\nCo-Authored-By: Codex (GPT-5) \u003ccodex@openai.com\u003e","files":null}]}